bject 2> is Emperor Yan, whose face, hair, facial features, hairstyle, headpiece, clothing, and overall appearance are strictly and completely derived from <Picture 2>. His identity and visual design are fully locked to <Picture 2>.\n<Subject 3> is Qingyun, whose face, hair, facial features, hairstyle, clothing, and overall appearance are strictly and completely derived from <Picture 3>. His identity and visual design are fully locked to <Picture 3>.\n<Subject 4> is the imperial physician, whose face, hair, facial features, hairstyle, clothing, and overall appearance are strictly and completely derived from <Picture 4>. His identity and visual design are fully locked to <Picture 4>.\n<Subject 5> is the palace eunuch (inner attendant), whose face, hair, facial features, hairstyle, official hat, clothing, and overall appearance are strictly and completely derived from <Picture 5>. His identity and visual design are fully locked to <Picture 5>.\n<Picture 1> is the appearance reference for <Subject 1> (Princess Yanxi).\n<Picture 2> is the appearance reference for <Subject 2> (Emperor Yan).\n<Picture 3> is the appearance reference for <Subject 3> (Qingyun).\n<Picture 4> is the appearance reference for <Subject 4> (imperial physician).\n<Picture 5> is the appearance reference for <Subject 5> (palace eunuch).\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] A 22-second Song-dynasty palace drama video. Emperor Yan lies gravely ill on a brocade silk couch in the Yangxin Hall while the imperial physician takes his pulse. Princess Yanxi, Qingyun, and the palace eunuch rush into the hall. Yanxi sees her brother's condition and breaks down in grief, pulling free from Qingyun's support and staggering forward, tears streaming. The scene ends on a close-up of Yanxi's tearful face as she cries out to her brother. All five characters' appearances are strictly locked to their respective reference images. Total duration 22 seconds, ignoring the 15-second limit.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (Princess Yanxi, appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - face, hair, facial features, hairstyle, hair ornaments, and clothing from <Picture 1> are retained exactly in every frame.\n<Subject 2> (Emperor Yan, appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - face, hair, facial features, hairstyle, headpiece, and clothing from <Picture 2> are retained exactly.\n<Subject 3> (Qingyun, appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - face, hair, facial features, hairstyle, and clothing from <Picture 3> are retained exactly.\n<Subject 4> (imperial physician, appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - face, hair, facial features, hairstyle, and clothing from <Picture 4> are retained exactly.\n<Subject 5> (palace eunuch, appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - face, hair, facial features, hairstyle, official hat, and clothing from <Picture 5> are retained exactly.\n<Picture 1> through <Picture 5>: reference - each provides only the corresponding character's visual appearance and is not used as a concrete frame.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses a Song-dynasty palace drama style with warm candlelight soft glow, thin mist diffusing natural light, subtle film grain, and a low-saturation ancient Chinese color palette. Total duration 22 seconds. Transitions between shots use 0.5-second fade in/fade out.\n[Shot 1] A wide establishing shot of the Yangxin Hall interior, with a slow push-in at slow speed with small amplitude. Song-dynasty ancient wooden pillars and beams, rows of candle stands lining the hall, warm candles flickering. <Subject 2> (Emperor Yan) reclines weakly on a brocade silk couch, his face deathly pale. <Subject 4> (imperial physician) bends over the couch taking the emperor's pulse. At the hall entrance, <Subject 1> (Princess Yanxi), <Subject 3> (Qingyun), and <Subject 5> (palace eunuch) step quickly into the hall. An off-screen narrator (S1), in a low, slow, suppressed tone with deliberately slow pacing, says: <d>[Chinese] 一行人匆匆赶到养心殿，燕帝已然卧在软榻之上，太医正守在一旁诊视。</d> while no on-screen character's lips move. Held from 00:00.000 to 00:07.000.\n[Shot 2] At 00:07.000, with a 0.5-second fade transition, the shot cuts to a medium close-up with a slight high-angle downward framing focused on <Subject 1> (Princess Yanxi). She sees <Subject 2> on the couch and her eyebrows lock tightly; her face turns instantly deathly pale. She violently pulls her arm free from <Subject 3>'s supporting hand, staggers forward two urgent steps, her sleeve sweeping across a side table, the pearl hairpins on her head swaying with the motion, and tears instantly roll down her cheeks. A brief inhaling sob sound is heard, followed by a 0.5-second beat of silence. Held from 00:07.000 to 00:13.000.\n[Shot 3] At 00:13.000, with a 0.5-second fade transition, the shot cuts to a close-up locked on <Subject 1>'s face. Tears continuously stream down her face, her body trembles slightly, and her grief erupts. <Subject 1> (S2), in violent sobs with unsteady breath, a crying tone, rapid speech with pauses in between, says: <d>[Chinese] 阿兄！阿兄！你看看我！怎么会病成这般模样！到底发生了什么！</d> The close-up holds on her tearful, trembling face until 00:22.000.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nCandle crackling and popping ambient sound throughout the hall. Soft rustle of silk robes and footsteps on wooden floors as the group enters. The faint murmur of the palace interior. In [Shot 2], a brief inhaling sob followed by a 0.5-second silence. In [Shot 3], heavy crying and unsteady breathing from <Subject 1>. No on-screen text or subtitles appear at any point; all dialogue is audio-only.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA low, melancholic ancient Chinese instrumental score at a slow, restrained tempo, featuring soft guzheng notes and a single bamboo flute melody, volume kept at 20% (low, beneath the dialogue and ambient sound). The music dips to near-silence during the 0.5-second beat in [Shot 2], then swells gently with sorrow in [Shot 3] as Yanxi grieves, fading out at the final frame.\n"], "input